.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH RANMA-POPUP 1 "" "ranma 0.1.0" "ranma manual"
.SH NAME
ranma\-popup \- Run a command in a float over this pane and print what it prints: \fBcd "$(ranma popup \-\- \*(Aqls ~/projects | fzf\*(Aq)"\fR. Waits for it, exits with its status, and gives focus back when it closes
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBranma popup\fR [\fB\-W\fR|\fB\-\-width\fR] [\fB\-H\fR|\fB\-\-height\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-title\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fICOMMAND\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a command in a float over this pane and print what it prints: \fBcd "$(ranma popup \-\- \*(Aqls ~/projects | fzf\*(Aq)"\fR. Waits for it, exits with its status, and gives focus back when it closes
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-W\fR, \fB\-\-width\fR \fI<WIDTH>\fR [default: 60]
Width in percent of the workspace
.TP
\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-height\fR \fI<HEIGHT>\fR [default: 60]
Height in percent of the workspace
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-title\fR \fI<TITLE>\fR
Name shown on its border
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fICOMMAND\fR>
The command. Its stdout is what \fBranma popup\fR prints, so the program must draw on the terminal itself (as fzf does), not on stdout
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBranma\fR(1)
